<GILES> Hehehe
<D.GARRETT> One thing we have (besides atrophy)...  is sparse
                    arrays.... any other language support such
                    array?
<GILES> U mean by that FEW arrays?  Or memory efficient arrays?
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> SmallTalk ... and ABC.
<D.GARRETT> ah
<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> A sparse array is one, almost all of whose
                    elements are 0 or null
<GILES> Ahso...thx, Len
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> Sparse arrays are a natural for OOP; in
                    programming you don't hav to know how the
                    array is implemented.
<D.GARRETT> well, in MUMPS we mean  that you can define X(1) and
                    X(999) and those two data nodes exist,
                    without declaring the rest of the array.
                    Memory efficient may be the correct term,
                    Giles.
<GILES> Ok...thx, Doug.
<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> Many versions of BASIC do the same.
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> Awk also.
<GILES> I don think so, Len...Not if...
<D.GARRETT> ah.... I thought I was all alone (with MUMPS) in that
